WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.466 --> 00:00:08.466
Hold on. Isn't that the...

2
00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:13.766
- Hm. We passed it before, right.
- Oh. That's so strange.

3
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.333
- I guess we're lost.
- Huh?

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.333
Hey, we went to the left last time, didn't we?

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.300
Pika, pika.

6
00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:25.933
Wow. You sure are good at getting scared.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.433
Have you ever heard the story about the scary house

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.133
that's supposed to be around here?

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.000
- Huh? Scary house?
- Uh-huh.

10
00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:37.866
It says if you go out of a certain forest at night time, a mansion appears.

11
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:42.133
If you go inside that mansion, you'll have the scariest experience of your life.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.866
- I wanna go.
- Denne-ne!

13
00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:48.000
You'd better be joking because I'm not going in a place like that.

14
00:00:48.066 --> 00:00:51.300
Yeah. I'd rather avoid it too, if at all possible.

15
00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:54.166
- What?
- So this time, let's go to the right.

16
00:00:54.233 --> 00:00:56.600
The Pokémon Centre's right past the forest.

17
00:00:56.666 --> 00:00:57.933
Pika!

18
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.900
- Wait up.
- Hey, don't leave me behind.

19
00:01:00.966 --> 00:01:03.366
We've gotta stick together, you know.

20
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.766
Uh-oh, a mansion!

21
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.900
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

22
00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:17.666
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

23
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:21.100
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

24
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:22.566
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

25
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:26.400
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

26
00:01:26.466 --> 00:01:29.666
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

27
00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:33.100
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

28
00:01:33.166 --> 00:01:37.066
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

29
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:41.766
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

30
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.033
♪ Pokémon! ♪

31
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.000
Scary Hospitality!

32
00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:55.266
Continuing to Laverre City,

33
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:58.100
our heroes have arrived at a mysterious mansion,

34
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:01.100
as though it had somehow drawn them there.

35
00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:03.900
Serena, so that's it?

36
00:02:03.966 --> 00:02:07.233
- Huh! It can't be.
- And the lights are on.

37
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.100
Then that means someone's gotta be living in there.

38
00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:13.366
Come on. It's just a story and nothing else.

39
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.500
Imagine somebody actually calling this the scary house.

40
00:02:16.566 --> 00:02:19.000
Hey, that's not fair.

41
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:21.800
- Pika. Brrr!
- Huh?

42
00:02:21.866 --> 00:02:24.733
- It's raining.
- Talk about bad timing.

43
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.433
- Good evening.
- Huh?

44
00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:30.733
What are you doing out there in that downpour?

45
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.300
- Hi, there. Is this the scary house?
- Uh! Bonnie!

46
00:02:34.366 --> 00:02:39.000
Scary house? Ah. I've heard of it being called that before,

47
00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:40.866
but it's just an ordinary house.

48
00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:45.266
- Too bad. It sounded like fun.
- Uh, I told you so, didn't I?

49
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:49.300
Please, you're all going to catch colds out there, so why don't you come in?

50
00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:52.166
- Thanks a lot.
- That's so nice.

51
00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:54.400
- There we go.
- This is great.

52
00:02:56.533 --> 00:02:58.400
- Wow. It's so big.
- Denne.

53
00:02:58.466 --> 00:03:00.800
You may use those towels over there.

54
00:03:00.866 --> 00:03:02.166
Thanks!

55
00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:04.933
- It's so fluffy.
- Denne-ne!

56
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.033
You're right.

57
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.533
Thank you so much. Here.

58
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.966
- Feels good, doesn't it?
- Pi, Pikachu!

59
00:03:12.866 --> 00:03:15.633
Strange. There are exactly enough towels for us.

60
00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.500
- Something wrong?
- Uh, heh, no, not at all.

61
00:03:18.566 --> 00:03:21.433
This towel is just so soft!

62
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.633
Well, now, my name is Lon.

63
00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.166
I'd like to know what all your names are. That is, if you wouldn't mind.

64
00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:29.200
Sure. Ash is my name.

65
00:03:29.266 --> 00:03:32.133
- And this is my partner, Pikachu.
- Pikachu.

66
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.700
- I'm Serena.
- My name's Bonnie.

67
00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:36.733
- This is Dedenne.
- Denne-ne.

68
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.500
- And this is my brother.
- I'm Clemont.

69
00:03:39.566 --> 00:03:41.666
I'm so sorry you got wet.

70
00:03:41.733 --> 00:03:44.733
How would you all like a nice hot dinner?

71
00:03:46.266 --> 00:03:48.700
- Awesome.
- Pika, pika.

72
00:03:48.766 --> 00:03:52.200
- Looks delicious.
- Looks yummy. I'm so hungry.

73
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.800
The right number of meals, also.

74
00:03:55.866 --> 00:03:58.900
It's as though he knew we were coming.

75
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.766
This is great!

76
00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.233
Mm. Mm.

77
00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:09.266
So good.

78
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.866
Pikachu.

79
00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:12.333
Pika, pika!

80
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.300
- Uh?
- Pika, pika!

81
00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:16.766
Chespin! Che, che, che...

82
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:19.200
Huh? Aren't you gonna eat with us, Lon?

83
00:04:19.266 --> 00:04:22.133
Oh, no. I've already eaten my dinner, thank you.

84
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.833
-Huh.

85
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.400
Wow. That was great.

86
00:04:31.466 --> 00:04:33.666
- Pika!
- Chespin, che!

87
00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:36.566
- Denne-ne!
- Thank you so much.

88
00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:40.733
Not only are we out of the rain, you've also given us such a delicious dinner.

89
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.266
Of course. I'm happy to help.

90
00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:45.433
I'm sure you'd do the same for me.

91
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.466
Now, why don't we all have a little after-dinner tea?

92
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.366
- All right.
- Sounds great. Yay.

93
00:04:50.433 --> 00:04:53.566
Why don't you wait in the living room?

94
00:04:53.633 --> 00:04:57.433
- Lon is such a nice person.
- Pika, pika.

95
00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.000
Calling this the scary house, how silly is that?

96
00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.400
You can't judge things by the way they look.

97
00:05:03.466 --> 00:05:04.466
Denne-ne!

98
00:05:04.533 --> 00:05:06.466
Still, we can't let our guard down.

99
00:05:08.266 --> 00:05:10.166
I don't think you've been noticing,

100
00:05:10.233 --> 00:05:12.566
but there have been some strange things going on.

101
00:05:12.633 --> 00:05:14.333
Strange things?

102
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.533
Chespin? Pin?

103
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.333
It looks like Lon is the only person who lives here in this old mansion,

104
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.966
so who got those fluffy towels ready?

105
00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:25.233
And who prepared all that delicious food?

106
00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.366
And don't you think it's strange he had the right number of towels and plates?

107
00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:31.100
It's as though he knew we were coming

108
00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:33.600
before we even arrived here in the first place.

109
00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.233
- Do you think?
- Pika?

110
00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.866
- Hm.
- Very strange.

111
00:05:37.933 --> 00:05:39.766
- Right this way.
- Uh?

112
00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:42.100
Your tea is ready.

113
00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.033
Excuse me. Do you have any idea why people would call this the scary house?

114
00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.133
Actually, I do know the reason for that.

115
00:05:53.866 --> 00:06:00.200
To tell the truth, I also arrived at this old house after losing my way.

116
00:06:00.266 --> 00:06:03.533
It was a cold, rainy evening.

117
00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:12.400
Excuse me. Is anyone home?

118
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.200
The electricity didn't appear to be working, but I had my own light.

119
00:06:20.266 --> 00:06:26.066
So, exhausted, I searched the dark house, finally arriving in the kitchen.

120
00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:31.333
Using my tiny flame, I slowly searched every inch of that room.

121
00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:36.866
Suddenly, I found a man hunched in the corner, sitting on the floor.

122
00:06:36.933 --> 00:06:39.866
I tried to approach and tell him I was lost,

123
00:06:39.933 --> 00:06:44.566
and ask if it would be OK if I spent the night here, out of the rain.

124
00:06:44.633 --> 00:06:46.866
- Then...
- Stay away!

125
00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.533
- I'm not talking to you.
- Huh?

126
00:06:54.566 --> 00:06:57.833
Not to me? I asked if somebody else was here.

127
00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.133
Then the man responded to me with this...

128
00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.000
- Don't you see them?
- Huh?

129
00:07:06.466 --> 00:07:09.866
The faceless men. They're standing right behind you!

130
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.933
-Pika!

131
00:07:19.066 --> 00:07:21.233
Hm!

132
00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.000
What do you think?

133
00:07:23.066 --> 00:07:25.500
Huh? What do you mean, what do we think?

134
00:07:25.566 --> 00:07:27.566
That was just awfully scary.

135
00:07:27.633 --> 00:07:29.266
- Serena's right.
- Pan, Pancham.

136
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:31.400
OK, then, what happened after that?

137
00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:34.533
Really? You're not even scared a little, Bonnie?

138
00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.433
- Nope.
- Ah, what do you know?

139
00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.533
I was hoping to entertain you all with the scariest story I could think of.

140
00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.900
But I guess I failed. Sorry.

141
00:07:42.966 --> 00:07:47.500
You see, I've told many visitors scary stories just like that one.

142
00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:49.200
Those stories are the reason

143
00:07:49.266 --> 00:07:52.133
this old mansion got to be known as the scary house.

144
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.733
Makes sense to me.

145
00:07:58.333 --> 00:07:59.966
Waaaah!

146
00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.400
- I assure you, I'm not doing this.
- All right, who is?

147
00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:08.500
- Yay. A ghost. Hello?
- Sounds paranormal to me.

148
00:08:08.566 --> 00:08:10.666
Ugh, this is not possible.

149
00:08:10.733 --> 00:08:14.033
There's not a thing science can't prove. Including this.

150
00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.700
Uh, then why don't you stop acting so scared already?

151
00:08:16.766 --> 00:08:20.633
Argh! That has nothing to do with this!

152
00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:25.033
Can science prove that? I would be very grateful.

153
00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.366
Of course. I guess that's my cue.

154
00:08:28.433 --> 00:08:33.100
The future is now, thanks to science. Clemontic Gear, on.

155
00:08:33.166 --> 00:08:37.333
I invented this device for precisely a situation like the one we have here.

156
00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.100
I call it my Mystery Watcher One.

157
00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:42.166
- Ah!
- It's a revolutionary machine

158
00:08:42.233 --> 00:08:45.366
that can detect and monitor unexplained mysterious powers

159
00:08:45.433 --> 00:08:48.633
by utilising comprehensive sensing technologies.

160
00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.966
- Hah! Science is so amazing.
- Pika!

161
00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:57.800
I suggest we search every room, starting with the second floor.

162
00:09:00.833 --> 00:09:02.366
- What's up?
- Pika?

163
00:09:02.433 --> 00:09:06.600
- It hasn't detected anything yet.
- Maybe your machine is broken.

164
00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.000
- What is it?
- Look.

165
00:09:13.666 --> 00:09:16.666
- The moon is out!
- So big and pretty.

166
00:09:16.733 --> 00:09:20.233
- Yeah. Rain's stopped. I sure am glad.
- Pika.

167
00:09:22.733 --> 00:09:24.666
- Pika.
- Huh?

168
00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:29.366
Ah! My shadow!

169
00:09:29.433 --> 00:09:32.766
- Clemont, use your machine.
- Good idea. Ugh!

170
00:09:35.233 --> 00:09:38.733
- Clemont?
- It's detecting something.

171
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.466
- Hey, what's happening?
- Pi...

172
00:09:41.533 --> 00:09:43.866
- It's suddenly getting chilly in here.
- Pikachu.

173
00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:46.866
It's over there. Unh!

174
00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.000
I am detecting something, but what is it?

175
00:09:53.466 --> 00:09:55.233
What was that? What was that? What was that?

176
00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.466
- A-ha.
- Yeah.

177
00:09:57.533 --> 00:09:59.166
Something's there, no doubt.

178
00:09:59.233 --> 00:10:03.033
If my machine detects something, but we can't see it, that means...

179
00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.466
-Pi...

180
00:10:04.533 --> 00:10:07.366
Right. There are ghosts living in this house.

181
00:10:07.433 --> 00:10:10.566
And those ghosts are all gathering around us right now.

182
00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:17.433
- Me and my big mouth.
- Hi, there, ghosts. I want to be friends.

183
00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.133
Who's that Pokémon?

184
00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.466
It's Gastly.

185
00:10:37.533 --> 00:10:39.600
Gastly.

186
00:10:50.966 --> 00:10:53.066
- Clemont?
- Yeah, right.

187
00:10:56.166 --> 00:11:00.066
I knew it. The ghosts are doing this.

188
00:11:00.133 --> 00:11:01.933
- Clemont!
- Pika, pika!

189
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.833
Maybe it's a poltergeist.

190
00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:08.600
Aah! This is a warning for me to stop trying to fight back with science.

191
00:11:08.666 --> 00:11:10.633
Wah!

192
00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:17.366
Oh, no, you don't. Give back my brother's machine.

193
00:11:17.433 --> 00:11:19.333
- Huh!
- Bonnie.

194
00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.833
Huh?

195
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:25.200
Now you settle down right this minute. Thank you.

196
00:11:25.266 --> 00:11:27.300
- Huh?
- Bonnie, are you all right?

197
00:11:29.266 --> 00:11:31.633
-Huh?

198
00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.733
The piano?

199
00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:36.800
Aah! Maybe that piano playing attracts even more of the ghosts

200
00:11:36.866 --> 00:11:38.400
who are living in this mansion.

201
00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.466
They take away lost boys and girls who wander into the scary house

202
00:11:43.533 --> 00:11:46.433
and then they disappear forever!

203
00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.333
-Ches!

204
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:52.600
Me and my big mouth again!

205
00:11:52.666 --> 00:11:54.966
-Pika!

206
00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.900
Hey, Clemont. Something's showing on the monitor.

207
00:11:59.966 --> 00:12:01.800
Huh?

208
00:12:06.733 --> 00:12:09.666
- Look at that.
- What do you know?

209
00:12:09.733 --> 00:12:11.533
Gastly.

210
00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.633
Gastly. The Gas Pokémon.

211
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:17.800
By enveloping larger opponents with gas, Gastly is able to defeat them.

212
00:12:19.433 --> 00:12:22.866
Haunter. The Gas Pokémon, and the evolved form of Gastly.

213
00:12:22.933 --> 00:12:25.333
Haunter can watch opponents by hiding in walls,

214
00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.300
and slips through anything in its way.

215
00:12:27.366 --> 00:12:31.566
Gengar. The Shadow Pokémon, and the evolved form of Haunter.

216
00:12:31.633 --> 00:12:35.233
Gengar is happy when it scares people, smiling wickedly in the dark.

217
00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.233
So they were doing all this stuff the whole time.

218
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.600
What do you think of their hospitality?

219
00:12:40.666 --> 00:12:43.100
That's what it is, you see.

220
00:12:43.166 --> 00:12:45.100
- Hospitality?
- Indeed.

221
00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:48.533
Gastly and the rest think scaring unsuspecting guests

222
00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.466
makes them feel at home.

223
00:12:50.533 --> 00:12:53.300
-Aah!

224
00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:57.300
So does that mean you're telling us you knew that they were here this whole time?

225
00:12:57.366 --> 00:13:00.866
Of course. Every one of them is a good friend.

226
00:13:00.933 --> 00:13:04.133
Ugh. I wish you had told us a bit sooner.

227
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.466
- Chespin. Chespin!
- Sooner?

228
00:13:07.533 --> 00:13:11.366
If I had told you, their hospitality would have been for nothing.

229
00:13:11.433 --> 00:13:14.400
That's the reason this house is called the scary house.

230
00:13:14.466 --> 00:13:16.366
-Haunter! Haunt, Haunter!

231
00:13:16.433 --> 00:13:18.833
Just as I said,

232
00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:22.366
paranormal activities can be proven otherwise with science.

233
00:13:22.433 --> 00:13:24.966
Ah. I was so scared.

234
00:13:25.033 --> 00:13:27.866
So there aren't any more scary things, right?

235
00:13:27.933 --> 00:13:30.866
Right. I'm glad you enjoyed the fun.

236
00:13:30.933 --> 00:13:33.866
It sure had a lot of realism.

237
00:13:33.933 --> 00:13:36.033
I'll bet Bonnie wishes it had been a ghost.

238
00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.833
- Bonnie?
- Pika!

239
00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.500
Huh? Where's Bonnie?

240
00:13:39.566 --> 00:13:42.100
She was right here just a minute ago.

241
00:13:42.166 --> 00:13:44.733
- Maybe Gengar hid her.
- Huh?

242
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.633
Gengar!

243
00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.133
- They're saying it wasn't them.
- Maybe she's back in the living room.

244
00:13:53.333 --> 00:13:55.866
- That was Ash.
- Pikachu.

245
00:13:57.033 --> 00:13:59.500
- Huh?
- Hey, Ash? Pikachu?

246
00:13:59.566 --> 00:14:02.066
Suddenly they're gone.

247
00:14:02.133 --> 00:14:06.066
- They have to be around here somewhere.
- We've got to find them.

248
00:14:07.766 --> 00:14:08.800
Uh! Huh?

249
00:14:08.866 --> 00:14:12.033
- Unh, Find anything?
- Hm.

250
00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.533
- Huh?
- Huh?

251
00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.566
- Aah!
- Hey! Serena.

252
00:14:16.633 --> 00:14:19.400
-Chespin, pin, pin.

253
00:14:19.466 --> 00:14:20.933
-Pin. Che.

254
00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.566
- What happened?
- She fell through the floor.

255
00:14:23.633 --> 00:14:27.500
Through the floor? Huh? Oh, no, no, no.

256
00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:31.366
- Hey, are you feeling all right, Lon?
- I'm thinking back.

257
00:14:31.433 --> 00:14:35.433
About another way to get downstairs or something like that.

258
00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:40.866
- Another way?
- Uh... Down to the basement.

259
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.333
- Right here.
- We've got to go down there too.

260
00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.600
-Are you sure you're feeling OK?

261
00:14:49.666 --> 00:14:52.766
It's just... I feel like I'm forgetting something.

262
00:14:52.833 --> 00:14:55.800
I think it's better if you wait here.

263
00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:05.033
I'll find you. Promise.

264
00:15:06.633 --> 00:15:10.166
Not scared. I'm not scared. I'm not scared.

265
00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.533
- Che! Che, che!
- Aaah! That door, it's sealed shut.

266
00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:22.133
But still, I've got to go.

267
00:15:28.666 --> 00:15:31.166
Why are those tags stuck all over the door?

268
00:15:31.233 --> 00:15:33.866
- Is that you, Clemont?
- It's Ash.

269
00:15:33.933 --> 00:15:36.500
- Clemont!
- Oh, Bonnie, you're in there too.

270
00:15:36.566 --> 00:15:38.333
Yeah. And Serena.

271
00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.533
We've been really trying to get out of here,

272
00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.033
but the door is so rusted, it won't budge.

273
00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.866
- Can you open it from your side?
- Pikachu?

274
00:15:45.933 --> 00:15:48.300
Stand by. Let me see.

275
00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:54.600
No. No good. Probably been shut for a long time.

276
00:15:54.666 --> 00:15:58.833
Wait. If it's rust, then Frogadier's Frubbles should do the trick.

277
00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:01.400
- Pika!
- You're right. What a great idea.

278
00:16:01.466 --> 00:16:03.900
Frogadier, I choose you.

279
00:16:05.333 --> 00:16:06.533
Froga!

280
00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:09.333
Frogadier, throw your Frubbles onto the door.

281
00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.300
Frogadier!

282
00:16:14.333 --> 00:16:17.300
Yes. Now.

283
00:16:22.466 --> 00:16:23.966
- You're all right!
- Big brother!

284
00:16:24.033 --> 00:16:25.733
Uh!

285
00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.500
- Were you scared?
- Mm-mm. I wasn't scared one bit.

286
00:16:29.566 --> 00:16:31.866
I knew Bonnie was gonna say that.

287
00:16:31.933 --> 00:16:34.766
- Were you scared? Tell the truth.
- Not me.

288
00:16:34.833 --> 00:16:38.300
Because I had a little sister to save.

289
00:16:39.933 --> 00:16:42.200
- Pika, pika!
- Huh?

290
00:16:45.133 --> 00:16:47.800
- Gastly.
- Here we are.

291
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:52.166
-Pika!

292
00:16:52.233 --> 00:16:55.166
It's good to see you. Glad you're safe.

293
00:16:55.233 --> 00:16:58.266
The trapdoors are all connected to a room in the basement.

294
00:16:58.333 --> 00:17:00.733
- Through hidden chutes.
- The basement?

295
00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.866
Yeah. The basement door had a bunch of tags pasted onto it.

296
00:17:03.933 --> 00:17:06.466
And we found this journal in the basement.

297
00:17:08.633 --> 00:17:12.466
You found a journal? Please read it to me.

298
00:17:12.533 --> 00:17:16.066
Sure. Let's see.

299
00:17:16.133 --> 00:17:18.233
"I was always afraid in this house,

300
00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.400
so I asked my dad to make a room in the basement

301
00:17:20.466 --> 00:17:22.266
that no one else could get into.

302
00:17:22.333 --> 00:17:27.566
- A super-secret room, just for me."
- That must be the room we got stuck in.

303
00:17:27.633 --> 00:17:30.233
"He even made me a bunch of cool passageways,

304
00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:33.266
so I could go to the room from anywhere in the house right away

305
00:17:33.333 --> 00:17:37.066
- when something was scaring me".
- Those are the trapdoors.

306
00:17:37.133 --> 00:17:39.100
But the scary things kept happening,

307
00:17:39.166 --> 00:17:43.466
so my dad finally brought a medium who could drive away the spirits of the house.

308
00:17:43.533 --> 00:17:48.066
Afterwards, he gave me a bunch of banishing tags to stick on my door."

309
00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:50.633
So that's what all those paper things were.

310
00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.066
They were placed there on the door for good luck.

311
00:17:53.133 --> 00:17:56.033
"Even so, scary things kept happening,

312
00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.500
so we're finally moving out of here today.

313
00:17:58.566 --> 00:18:03.566
- This is my last day in the house."
- Huh?

314
00:18:06.433 --> 00:18:08.800
I wonder if the writer is this boy.

315
00:18:10.866 --> 00:18:14.066
Hey. He kind of looks like you, don't you think?

316
00:18:14.133 --> 00:18:20.233
Oh. Ah, right. How could I have forgotten? That is me.

317
00:18:21.466 --> 00:18:23.100
What are you talking about?

318
00:18:23.166 --> 00:18:27.000
Well, I completely forgot about that room

319
00:18:27.066 --> 00:18:30.166
and how I put up all of those paper good luck charms.

320
00:18:30.233 --> 00:18:32.166
- Gastly.
- Gengar, Gengar.

321
00:18:32.233 --> 00:18:34.166
Really?

322
00:18:34.233 --> 00:18:40.133
So it was you, Gastly, Haunter, and Gengar, behind all those incidents.

323
00:18:42.666 --> 00:18:47.100
Back then, all you wanted to do was play and have a little fun.

324
00:18:47.166 --> 00:18:51.033
And yet, my family thought it was something completely different,

325
00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.566
and so we moved.

326
00:18:53.633 --> 00:18:58.133
Of course. It now seems so simple.

327
00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.433
I apologise.

328
00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.100
- Gastly.
- Gengar!

329
00:19:03.266 --> 00:19:05.333
Huh?

330
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.966
Hey, look. There's a date on the back of this picture.

331
00:19:10.266 --> 00:19:14.800
Huh? Ah! That picture was taken over 200 years ago.

332
00:19:15.766 --> 00:19:19.200
It's all coming back to me now.

333
00:19:21.766 --> 00:19:24.700
Well, you see, I'm not quite alive.

334
00:19:24.766 --> 00:19:26.766
- Pika!

335
00:19:36.766 --> 00:19:39.633
- Hey. What's this?
- Aah.

336
00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:43.333
- Weren't we just in the scary house?
- And where's Lon?

337
00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.200
- Huh?
- Uh? And those three Pokémon?

338
00:19:46.266 --> 00:19:50.333
Maybe you guys spend so much time together that now you have the same dreams.

339
00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:51.433
Denne, denne.

340
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.833
- Come on.
- Yeah, no way.

341
00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.766
Was it a dream?

342
00:19:54.833 --> 00:19:58.700
Hey, look. The Pokémon Centre. Hurry, hurry.

343
00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.633
Ne. Denne.

344
00:20:11.833 --> 00:20:15.666
And so, scary house history repeats itself again and again,

345
00:20:15.733 --> 00:20:18.800
as the journey continues.

346
00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:25.700
- Great time to get lost.
- And in a downpour.

347
00:20:25.766 --> 00:20:28.533
- What a bore.
- Wobbuffet.

348
00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:30.466
Wob. Wobba!

349
00:20:33.066 --> 00:20:38.033
Good evening. What are you doing out there in that downpour?

350
00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:42.500
Please, you're all going to catch colds out there, so why don't you come in?
